sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User
    participant UI as Browser copilot
    participant API as routes/assistant.py
    participant Planner as agent_processor + planner
    participant Memory as Skills + local memory
    participant LLM as Optional loopback model
    participant Worker as app.py background worker
    participant Engine as Executor + processors
    User->>UI: Select media and describe edit
    UI->>API: POST /api/agent/upload (or chunk + complete)
    API-->>UI: Media identifier and inspected context
    UI->>API: POST /api/agent/chat
    API->>Planner: query_agent_orchestrator(...)
    Planner->>Memory: Skill expansion / relevant context
    opt Local reasoning selected and available
        Planner->>LLM: Budgeted structured planning request
        LLM-->>Planner: Proposed plan
    end
    Note over Planner: Validate tools, arguments, media types and dependencies
    Planner-->>API: Validated plan or clarification
    alt Clarification needed
        API-->>UI: JSON clarification options
    else Short edit
        API->>Engine: execute_agent_plan(...)
        Engine-->>API: Verified outputs / per-step results
        API->>Memory: Queue chat observation
        API-->>UI: JSON result and artifact URLs
    else Long edit
        API-->>UI: Background-job confirmation prompt
        User->>UI: Confirm
        UI->>API: POST /api/agent/job/submit
        API->>Worker: Start daemon thread
        API-->>UI: job_id
        Worker->>Engine: execute_agent_plan(...)
        loop While browser waits
            UI->>API: GET /api/agent/job/{job_id}
            API-->>UI: In-memory job status
        end
        opt User requests cancellation
            UI->>API: POST /api/agent/job/{job_id}/cancel
            API->>Worker: Set cancellation flag
        end
        Engine-->>Worker: Results or failure
        Note over Worker: Current worker checks cancellation after executor returns
        UI->>API: GET /api/agent/job/{job_id}
        API-->>UI: Final status and output URL
    end
    UI->>API: GET /processed/{filename}
    API-->>User: Download / preview output
